gomodel:6ab067da00010366
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "PTEN lipid phosphatase activity (GO:0016314) is drawn causally upstream of, negative effect, CTNNB1 at the curator's choice. Caveat: Bae 2021 (PMID:33428810) PtenDeltaC lacks the PDZ-binding motif but keeps normal AKT/mTOR phosphorylation (Fig EV1G) and still shows more nuclear beta-catenin (Fig 2D, 2F), so the effect may not need the phosphatase activity." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. Revised version of gomodel:62900b6400001630 (PTEN in NMDAR-dependent LTD) following review of 2026-10-22: ISS evidence moved to GO_REF:0000024 with RGD/MGI orthologs; PTEN-to-beta-catenin edge moved to a separate PTEN unit (PDZ-binding-motif role, PMID:33428810); SLC6A20 negatively regulates NMDAR via glycine clearance." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "development" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-22" ;
        dc:title               "PTEN in excitatory hippocampal synapse long-term depression (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00010366 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

